  "scope": "# Review return \u2014 83ca9df09514\n\nTask `83ca9df09514`; selected production generator remains version `3.0.1`, SHA-256 `70db137b815d1463c9b759c9258749291aef361633d91fbf64e7c72c8d6f2233`.\nBuilt a **proposed, unapproved** task-local parameter prototype: `duplicate_precedence \u2208 {rightmost_wins, leftmost_wins}`.\nThe canonical/default `rightmost_wins` program is byte-identical to canonical Racket SHA-256 `cae56e2f8161ccd2fd21aa8b0d4e0b51318d3e114e626ea9097fab7c2602af87`, rule hash `1dc6f00b70c9`.\nThe alternate changes exactly one mapping-loop traversal; production generator, canonical data, catalog metadata, approval state, and shared runtime were not changed.\nRetained two paired episodes, each with 2 demonstrations and 4 distinct queries; demonstrations alone identify the setting against the opposite precedence rule.\nPublic challenge IDs hash only visible bytes; seeds, settings, programs, rivals, and query answers remain private.\nVerification: **68/68 task-local tests passed**, including six new behavior tests; all ten source-qualified canonical pairs replay under the default.\nAdversarial pass: 16/16 maximum-count paired inputs distinct and setting-separating in Racket; exact one-loop mutation and tamper rejection passed.\nRemaining limit: conflicting duplicate keys extend production grammar, and finite evidence distinguishes only the two declared settings; this does not approve production or training use.\nDisposition: routine prototype review, with maintainer attention needed only for the product decision about admitting conflicting duplicate keys.",
